Find the largest candy count once. Kid `i` ends up with the greatest number exactly when `candies[i] + extraCandies` is at least that maximum, so compare each kid against it.

This runs in O(n) time and uses O(n) space for the result array.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {number[]} candies
 * @param {number} extraCandies
 * @return {boolean[]}
 */
var kidsWithCandies = function(candies, extraCandies) {
    const mx = Math.max(...candies);
    return candies.map(c => c + extraCandies >= mx);
};
