Use prefix sums for rows, columns and both diagonals so each line sum in a candidate square is an O(1) lookup.

**Prefix arrays** (all 1-indexed, size `(m+1) x (n+1)`):
- `row[i][j+1] = row[i][j] + grid[i][j]`
- `col[i+1][j] = col[i][j] + grid[i][j]`
- Main diagonal, indexed by the cell just past the end: `d1[i+1][j+1] = d1[i][j] + grid[i][j]`.
- Anti-diagonal, indexed `a[i+1][j] = a[i][j+1] + grid[i][j]`. Here `a[i+1][j]` is the sum of the cells going up-right from `(i, j)`.

**Line sums for a square** with top-left `(r, c)` and size `k`:
- Main diagonal: `d1[r+k][c+k] - d1[r][c]`.
- Anti-diagonal: it runs from `(r, c+k-1)` down-left to `(r+k-1, c)`.
  - Via the recurrence, `a[r+k][c]` covers cells `(r+k-1, c)`, `(r+k-2, c+1)`, … going up-right.
  - Subtract `a[r][c+k]`, which covers `(r-1, c+k)` and further up-right.
  - So the anti-diagonal sum is `a[r+k][c] - a[r][c+k]`.

**Search order:** try `k` from `min(m, n)` down to 2. For each position, compute the target from the main diagonal and check the anti-diagonal, every row and every column, exiting early on a mismatch. Return the first `k` that works, or 1 if none does.

**Cost:** O(m·n·min(m, n)²), about 50⁴ ≈ 6M operations, which is fine.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {number[][]} grid
 * @return {number}
 */
var largestMagicSquare = function(grid) {
    const m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;
    const mk = () => Array.from({length: m + 1}, () => new Array(n + 2).fill(0));
    const row = mk(), col = mk(), d1 = mk(), a = mk();
    for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) {
        for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            const v = grid[i][j];
            row[i][j + 1] = row[i][j] + v;
            col[i + 1][j] = col[i][j] + v;
            d1[i + 1][j + 1] = d1[i][j] + v;
            a[i + 1][j] = a[i][j + 1] + v;
        }
    }
    for (let k = Math.min(m, n); k >= 2; k--) {
        for (let r = 0; r + k <= m; r++) {
            for (let c = 0; c + k <= n; c++) {
                const target = d1[r + k][c + k] - d1[r][c];
                if (a[r + k][c] - a[r][c + k] !== target) continue;
                let ok = true;
                for (let i = r; i < r + k && ok; i++) {
                    if (row[i][c + k] - row[i][c] !== target) ok = false;
                }
                for (let j = c; j < c + k && ok; j++) {
                    if (col[r + k][j] - col[r][j] !== target) ok = false;
                }
                if (ok) return k;
            }
        }
    }
    return 1;
};
```

