Remove the dashes and uppercase everything. The first group gets whatever is left over, `n % k` characters (or a full `k` if `n` divides evenly). After that, take chunks of exactly `k` and join all groups with dashes. If no characters remain after removing dashes, return an empty string.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {string} s
 * @param {number} k
 * @return {string}
 */
var licenseKeyFormatting = function(s, k) {
    const t = s.replace(/-/g, '').toUpperCase();
    const n = t.length;
    if (n === 0) return '';
    const parts = [];
    let first = n % k;
    if (first === 0) first = k;
    parts.push(t.slice(0, first));
    for (let i = first; i < n; i += k) {
        parts.push(t.slice(i, i + k));
    }
    return parts.join('-');
};
```

