Approach: for each infected node `u`, find the clean (non-infected) nodes that only `u` can reach. Removing `u` saves exactly those nodes.

1. For each infected node `u`, run a DFS from `u` that moves only through non-infected nodes.
2. Every clean node reached this way records `u` as one of its infectors.
3. A clean node with exactly one infector is saved when that infector is removed. Credit that infector with +1.
4. Return the infected node with the highest count. Ties go to the smallest index, so I sort `initial` first and only replace the answer on a strictly larger count.

This works because removing `u` deletes it and all its edges. Any clean node that some other infected node can still reach through clean nodes stays infected. A node reachable only via `u` through clean nodes becomes safe.

Complexity: each DFS is O(n²) on the adjacency matrix, so the total is O(k·n²) for `k` infected nodes. That is about 27M operations in the worst case, which is fine.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {number[][]} graph
 * @param {number[]} initial
 * @return {number}
 */
var minMalwareSpread = function(graph, initial) {
    const n = graph.length;
    const infected = new Uint8Array(n);
    for (const u of initial) infected[u] = 1;
    const cnt = new Int32Array(n);
    const who = new Int32Array(n).fill(-1);
    for (const u of initial) {
        const seen = new Uint8Array(n);
        seen[u] = 1;
        const stack = [u];
        while (stack.length) {
            const x = stack.pop();
            const row = graph[x];
            for (let y = 0; y < n; y++) {
                if (row[y] === 1 && !seen[y] && !infected[y]) {
                    seen[y] = 1;
                    stack.push(y);
                    cnt[y]++;
                    who[y] = u;
                }
            }
        }
    }
    const save = new Int32Array(n);
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        if (!infected[i] && cnt[i] === 1) save[who[i]]++;
    }
    const sorted = [...initial].sort((a, b) => a - b);
    let best = sorted[0];
    for (const u of sorted) {
        if (save[u] > save[best]) best = u;
    }
    return best;
};
```

