Treat each pair of points as possible opposite (diagonal) corners of a rectangle:

1. Put every point into a set, encoded as `x * 40001 + y`. Since coordinates are at most 40000, this key is unique per point.
2. For each pair of points `p` and `q`, skip the pair if they share an x or a y coordinate, because then they cannot be diagonal corners.
3. Otherwise, the other two corners must be `(x1, y2)` and `(x2, y1)`. If both are in the set, the pair forms a rectangle with area `|x1 - x2| * |y1 - y2|`; keep the minimum.
4. If no rectangle is found, return 0.

With n ≤ 500, the O(n²) loop over pairs is about 125,000 iterations, which is fast enough.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {number[][]} points
 * @return {number}
 */
var minAreaRect = function(points) {
    const set = new Set();
    for (const [x, y] of points) set.add(x * 40001 + y);
    let best = Infinity;
    const n = points.length;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const [x1, y1] = points[i];
        for (let j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            const [x2, y2] = points[j];
            if (x1 === x2 || y1 === y2) continue;
            const area = Math.abs(x1 - x2) * Math.abs(y1 - y2);
            if (area >= best) continue;
            if (set.has(x1 * 40001 + y2) && set.has(x2 * 40001 + y1)) {
                best = area;
            }
        }
    }
    return best === Infinity ? 0 : best;
};
```

