- On `'['`, increment `open`.
- On `']'`, if `open > 0`, it matches an earlier `'['`, so decrement `open`.
- Otherwise the `']'` has no match; count it in `unmatched`.

After the scan, `unmatched` is the number of `']'` that can never be matched. One swap of an unmatched `']'` with a later `'['` fixes two unmatched pairs at once. So the answer is `ceil(unmatched / 2)`.

