Represent which letters of `target` are still needed as a bitmask over its positions, then run a BFS or DP over masks.

1. Let `n = target.length`, so there are `2^n` masks (at most 32768). Set `dp[0] = 0` and every other entry to infinity.
2. Process masks in increasing order. For each reachable mask and each sticker:
   - Copy the sticker's letter counts.
   - Walk the positions of `target`. For each position not yet covered, if the sticker still has that letter, cover the position and decrement the count.
   - This gives a new mask; relax `dp[new] = min(dp[new], dp[mask] + 1)`.
3. Applying a sticker only ever adds bits, so the new mask is always larger than the current one. That makes increasing-order processing valid.

**Pruning.** For each mask, find the first uncovered position. Only try stickers that contain that letter. Some sticker must eventually cover it, and the order in which stickers are applied doesn't matter, so this loses no solutions.

**Greedy fill is safe.** When a sticker is applied, it fills the earliest uncovered positions of each letter. Positions holding the same letter are interchangeable, so which ones get covered does not change the reachable outcomes.

**Cost.** At most 32768 masks × 50 stickers × 15 positions, about 24M operations, which is fine.

**Answer.** Return `dp[full]` if it is finite, otherwise `-1`.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {string[]} stickers
 * @param {string} target
 * @return {number}
 */
var minStickers = function(stickers, target) {
    const n = target.length;
    const full = (1 << n) - 1;
    const cnts = stickers.map(s => {
        const c = new Array(26).fill(0);
        for (const ch of s) c[ch.charCodeAt(0) - 97]++;
        return c;
    });
    const t = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) t.push(target.charCodeAt(i) - 97);
    const INF = 1e9;
    const dp = new Int32Array(1 << n).fill(INF);
    dp[0] = 0;
    const tmp = new Array(26);
    for (let mask = 0; mask < full; mask++) {
        if (dp[mask] === INF) continue;
        let first = -1;
        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (!(mask & (1 << i))) { first = i; break; }
        }
        const fl = t[first];
        for (const c of cnts) {
            if (c[fl] === 0) continue;
            for (let k = 0; k < 26; k++) tmp[k] = c[k];
            let nm = mask;
            for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if (!(nm & (1 << i)) && tmp[t[i]] > 0) {
                    tmp[t[i]]--;
                    nm |= (1 << i);
                }
            }
            if (dp[mask] + 1 < dp[nm]) dp[nm] = dp[mask] + 1;
        }
    }
    return dp[full] === INF ? -1 : dp[full];
};
```

