The idea is to store the words reversed in a trie and walk it backwards over the most recent characters of the stream.

**Building the trie**
- Insert every word in reverse order.
- Mark the node where a reversed word ends as terminal.
- Keep the trie in flat typed arrays. The node count is bounded by the total number of characters plus one, so we can preallocate exactly.

**Keeping the stream**
- Store only the last `maxLen` characters (at most 200) in a circular buffer, where `maxLen` is the longest word length.
- No suffix longer than that can match a word.

**Answering a query**
- Push the new letter into the buffer.
- Walk the trie from the newest character backwards.
- Return `true` as soon as we reach a terminal node.
- Return `false` if the path breaks or we run out of buffered characters.

**Complexity**
- Each query costs O(maxLen) ≤ 200 steps, so 4·10⁴ queries is about 8·10⁶ steps.
- Building the trie is O(total characters).

**Input handling**
Only characters `a`–`z` are used, so stray spaces in the input are ignored.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {string[]} words
 */
var StreamChecker = function(words) {
    let total = 1, maxLen = 1;
    const ws = [];
    for (const w of words) {
        const codes = [];
        for (let i = 0; i < w.length; i++) {
            const c = w.charCodeAt(i) - 97;
            if (c >= 0 && c < 26) codes.push(c);
        }
        ws.push(codes);
        total += codes.length;
        if (codes.length > maxLen) maxLen = codes.length;
    }
    this.child = new Int32Array(total * 26);
    this.end = new Uint8Array(total);
    let cnt = 1;
    for (const codes of ws) {
        let node = 0;
        for (let i = codes.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            const idx = node * 26 + codes[i];
            if (this.child[idx] === 0) this.child[idx] = cnt++;
            node = this.child[idx];
        }
        this.end[node] = 1;
    }
    this.maxLen = maxLen;
    this.buf = new Int32Array(maxLen);
    this.pos = 0;
    this.size = 0;
};

/** 
 * @param {character} letter
 * @return {boolean}
 */
StreamChecker.prototype.query = function(letter) {
    let c = -1;
    for (let i = 0; i < letter.length; i++) {
        const x = letter.charCodeAt(i) - 97;
        if (x >= 0 && x < 26) { c = x; break; }
    }
    if (c < 0) return false;
    const m = this.maxLen;
    this.buf[this.pos] = c;
    this.pos = (this.pos + 1) % m;
    if (this.size < m) this.size++;
    let node = 0;
    let p = this.pos;
    const child = this.child, end = this.end, buf = this.buf;
    for (let k = 0; k < this.size; k++) {
        p = p - 1;
        if (p < 0) p += m;
        node = child[node * 26 + buf[p]];
        if (node === 0) return false;
        if (end[node]) return true;
    }
    return false;
};

/** 
 * Your StreamChecker object will be instantiated and called as such:
 * var obj = new StreamChecker(words)
 * var param_1 = obj.query(letter)
 */
```

