The approach is a column-by-column backtracking search, working from the rightmost digit leftward, similar to doing the addition by hand.

1. **Quick rejection.** If any word is longer than `result`, the sum must have more digits than `result`, so return `false`. The inputs are also trimmed to drop stray whitespace.

2. **Leading-zero set.** Record the first character of every multi-character word, and of `result` if it has more than one character. These characters may not be assigned 0.

3. **Search state `dfs(col, row, sum)`.**
   - `col` is the current column, counted from the right.
   - `row` is the current word index.
   - `sum` is the running column total, which starts as the carry from the previous column.

4. **Steps within a column.**
   - For each word that has a character in this column, use its digit if already assigned. Otherwise try every unused digit, respecting the leading-zero rule.
   - After all words are processed, the `result` character in this column must equal `sum % 10`.
     - If that character is already assigned, it must match.
     - If it is unassigned, that digit must be free and must not break the leading-zero rule.
   - Move to the next column with carry `floor(sum / 10)`.

5. **Termination.** After the last column of `result`, the equation holds only if the remaining carry is 0.

Checking each column as soon as it is complete prunes invalid partial assignments early. This keeps the search fast for at most 10 distinct letters.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {string[]} words
 * @param {string} result
 * @return {boolean}
 */
var isSolvable = function(words, result) {
    words = words.map(w => w.trim());
    result = result.trim();
    const R = result.length;
    for (const w of words) if (w.length > R) return false;
    const leading = new Set();
    for (const w of words) if (w.length > 1) leading.add(w[0]);
    if (R > 1) leading.add(result[0]);
    const val = {};
    const used = new Array(10).fill(false);
    const n = words.length;
    const ch = (s, col) => s[s.length - 1 - col];

    const dfs = (col, row, sum) => {
        if (col === R) return sum === 0;
        if (row === n) {
            const c = ch(result, col);
            const d = sum % 10;
            const carry = Math.floor(sum / 10);
            if (val[c] !== undefined) {
                if (val[c] !== d) return false;
                return dfs(col + 1, 0, carry);
            }
            if (used[d]) return false;
            if (d === 0 && leading.has(c)) return false;
            val[c] = d; used[d] = true;
            const ok = dfs(col + 1, 0, carry);
            delete val[c]; used[d] = false;
            return ok;
        }
        const w = words[row];
        if (col >= w.length) return dfs(col, row + 1, sum);
        const c = ch(w, col);
        if (val[c] !== undefined) return dfs(col, row + 1, sum + val[c]);
        for (let d = 0; d < 10; d++) {
            if (used[d]) continue;
            if (d === 0 && leading.has(c)) continue;
            val[c] = d; used[d] = true;
            const ok = dfs(col, row + 1, sum + d);
            delete val[c]; used[d] = false;
            if (ok) return true;
        }
        return false;
    };
    return dfs(0, 0, 0);
};
